outcome:
After sync, every TermAl test module has a concrete review verdict, led by Kimi::Consultant with the TermAl team. For each module or test group the review records:
- what it protects;
- whether it checks real observable behaviour, or is brittle or tied to code details;
- its cost (runtime, timeouts, benchmark-like behaviour);
- duplicates;
- a recommendation, DELETE, SIMPLIFY or KEEP, with the reason.
The prioritised findings become follow-up items with owners. No new gate is added.
